# WHAT A YARD IS WORTH WALKING INTO (docs/VISION.md §9.5, §10.4). The plan has
# carried somebody off, and the region stops asking him about its ground and
# starts asking him about a person. The same three housings, the same steel edge,
# the same dark yard as tours/works.tour — and this time somebody walks out of it
# and somebody at the village says so.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/rescue.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --held=axe_felling --carried=1
#
# `--carried=1` stages what hours of real play would: one person held at the
# first depot of the plan that has a village in its region (45_taken), because a
# rescue needs both halves — a yard to put dark and somebody left who knew them.
# `at rescue:asker` is that village and `at rescue:yard` is that depot: named, never a
# coordinate and never an index, because `place works` is the first depot
# anywhere on the island and the plan does not take people to it out of politeness.

coast calm
at rescue:asker
wait 2.5
at rescue:somebody
wait 0.4

# THE ASK. Whoever is in front of him lives here, and what they have to say is
# what the region has to say: not the yard, not the ground, the neighbour who was
# taken out of a door in the morning. "A yard that's dark doesn't hold anybody"
# is the whole of the teaching — no marker, no task line, no arrow.
press use
await talking 4
wait 0.5
shot 01-somebody-asks-after-a-neighbour with talking,folk
# And he says he will, because what they say at the end is about what he said
# here: saying nothing is always the other answer and is never punished.
tap use
wait 0.6
await heard_ask:rescue 3

# THE YARD, and the reason it is not a number any more. It is the most dangerous
# ground in a landscape and it was always the most important, and only now can
# anybody say why.
at rescue:yard
wait 1.0
await held_here 6
shot 02-the-yard-that-is-holding-them with works,works_lit,works_yard

# THE ONE ACT. Three housings, three walks, a steel edge and the key held — the
# same thing tours/works.tour proves, doing three things at once: half of a
# chapter's DEFENDED, the region quiet for good, and the door open.
press use 5.5
await works_part 14
at rescue:yard_breaker
wait 0.5
press use 5.5
await works_open:2 14
at rescue:yard_coolant
wait 0.5
press use 5.5
await works_broken 14
wait 0.6
await freed 6
shot 03-the-yard-goes-dark-and-they-walk-out with works,works_dark

# THE THANKS. Back at the village, and this is the line the package could not
# say for its whole life: the act that answers a goal is the act that stops the
# goal being raised, so the region used to greet him with the next errand.
at rescue:asker
wait 2.5
at rescue:somebody
wait 0.4
press use
await talking 4
await thanked:rescue 4
wait 0.5
shot 04-he-said-he-would-and-they-say-he-did with talking,folk
press pause
wait 0.5
